===Etymology===
{{inh+|en|enm|relicte|t=widow}}, from {{der|en|frm|relicte|t=widow}}, from {{der|en|LL.|relicta|t=widow}}, from {{der|en|la|relictus}}, past participle of {{m|la|relinquō||I abandon, I relinquish, I leave (behind)}}, from {{m|la|re-}} + {{m|la|linquō||I leave, quit, forsake, depart from}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛlɪkt/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-relict.wav|Audio (UK)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|formal}} Something that, or someone who, survives or remains or is left over after the loss of others; a [[relic]].
## {{lb|en|archaic}} The [[survive|surviving]] member of a married couple after one or the other has died; a [[widow]] or [[widower]].
##* '''1801''', in the ''Reports of cases decided in the High court of Chancery of Maryland'', volume 3, page 268:
##*: {{quote|en|Upon which the Chancellor, by way of note said, 'it is suggested, that there is a '''relict''' of the deceased, married to another man, who has joined her in a power of attorney to authorize the sale of her interest, {{...}}'}}
##* {{quote-book|en|1973|Patrick O'Brian|HMS Surprise|text=But I am not the penniless nonentity I was when we first met; I can offer an honorable if not a brilliant marriage; and at the very lowest I can provide my wife – my widow, my '''relict''' – with a ''decent competence'', an assured future.}}
## {{lb|en|biology|ecology}} A [[species]], [[organism]]{{,}} or [[ecosystem]] that has survived from a previous age: one that was once widespread but is now found only in a few areas.
##* {{quote-book|en|2010|M. Zimmerman et al.|'''Relict''' Species: Phylogeography and Conservation Biology|editor=Jan Christian Habel, Thorsten Assmann|page=324|text=The species may be a '''relict''' of former stages of historical vegetation and landscape development resulting from past climate changes (glacial and post- glacial periods).}}
## {{lb|en|geology}} A [[structure]] or other feature that has survived from a previous age.
##* {{quote-book|en|2011|Mark Keiter, Chris Ballhaus, Frank Tomaschek|A New Geological Map of the Island of Syros (Aegean Sea, Greece)|page=16|text=Dark rims around the pillows are caused by glaucophane enrichment, possibly a '''relict''' of a primary interaction between basalt and seawater, causing Na- enrichment in the original glass crust of the pillows.}}
## {{lb|en|linguistics}} A survival of an [[archaic]] word, language or other form.
##: {{ux|en|A small number of linguists believe that Cimbrian is not an Austro-Bavarian dialect but a '''relict''' of Lombardic.}}

